			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Restore 1400+ closing parentheses stripped by prior bulk refactor\n\nThe prior `)` → `;` bulk statement-termination refactor from the Effect-TS removal erroneously stripped the closing `)` from practically every call expression across ~140 files in the Cocoon extension host — codegen emitters, ESBuild/Mountain config, IPC channel/handler/protocol, platform environment/OS/process detection, patch-process loader/patcher/security/validator, effect-service bootstrap/extension/health/module-interceptor/mountain-client/rpc-server/telemetry, all VS Code API handler namespaces (authentication, commands, comments, debug, env, extensions, languages, scm, tasks, tests, window, workspace), document-content handler, extension-host handler, language-provider handler, notification handler, request-routing handler, service implementations (command, configuration, dev-log, dual-track, echo-action, error-handling, extension, file-system, health, language-provider-registry, logger, metrics-collector, module-interceptor, mountain-client, performance-monitoring, security, window-dialog/errors/file-dialogs/quick-input/state/status-bar/text-document/webview-panel, workspace), gRPC server, Node module interceptor shim, telemetry (OTLP bridge, PostHog buffer/config/event/transport), type converters (command, dialog, main markdown/range/text-edit/URI/view-column, quick-input, task, tree-view, webview-option, workspace-edit), utility (event-stream, glob-to-regex, land-fix-log, tier), webview panel (factory, message, panel, serializer, state, webview implementation), and the prepublish build script.\n\nRestore `)` before `;` in every affected expression — `parseInt`, `FormatOutput`, `Error` constructors, `Map` allocations, `Set` allocations, `JSON.stringify`, `throw new Error`, `errors.push`, `Option.some/none`, `Date.now`, `Symbol.for`, `Context.GenericTag`, `EventSubscriber`, `.join()`, dynamic `import()`, `setTimeout`, `clearTimeout`, `Socket.once`, `createConnection`, `Path.resolve`, `RegExp`, `mountainClient.sendRequest`, `CocoonDevLog`, `process.stdout.write`, `process.stderr.write`, `mkdir`, `writeFile`, `Reflect.construct`, `Object.setPrototypeOf`, `.split()`, `.filter()`, `.includes()`, `.toUpperCase()`, `.toLowerCase()`, `.bind()`, `.unref()`, `new URL()`, `new TextEncoder()`, `createRequire`, `fileURLToPath`, `dirname`, `uuidv4`, `setImmediate`, `setInterval`, `clearInterval`, `Emitter.on/off/once`, `Layer.sync`, `Effect.suspend`, and all other call, constructor, method-invocation, and arrow-expression boundary sites.\n\nA Python helper script (`fix_mountain.py`) is committed alongside the manual fixes to automate repeated `parseInt`/`errors.push` patterns in the Mountain config reader.\n\nAll call expressions now compile with balanced parentheses and valid TypeScript statement syntax — completing the same fix pattern applied across the other Cocoon modules in the preceding four commits.",
			"SHA": "1bf998ce9768c83d1ff486c3a0fa28ded9469649"
